Also Nvidia learned the lesson of the 10 series, they do not ever want to make a ti card too good ever again.

 @YarbroughJL82  But it is how economics work, supply is low demand is high, prices go up, supply high demand low prices drop, it's a universal constant of economics. 

Yes, some governments outlaw it during emergencies, but prices are kept in check via competition in normal circumstances. If one company's prices are too high, you go to the other company. 

We're not under emergency circumstances as far as being gamers go for GPUs, and there is a global breakdown of the supply chain due to unprecedented demand and a pandemic that crippled shipping across the entire world.  So prices are out of control.

