 @jamescampbell8482  You should watch the WAN show where Linus and Luke address this. They actually have a terrible relationship with Nvidia, which makes comments like this laughable to them. Nvidia MSRP is an arbitrary number. They don't set the final pricing. Nvidia only manufactures the chips. Board partners and retailers are the ones who actually manufacture and sell the GPUs. THEY set the actual prices. With current scalping practices, we're seeing prices often x2 or more over that MSRP because board partners, retailers, 3rd party sellers and scalpers have all driven the prices up while recognizing the lack of availability due to many other manufacturing struggles such as the continued extreme drought in Taiwan. Many, many factors have contributed to these price hikes. All Linus & Co have been saying is that in this climate, at this time, where availability is just one factor of many, if you can find a card even close to MSRP and you have the money, it IS a good deal and you should buy it.

WAN show explanation video
https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PkJYWMStLRA

